course: dictionary
lesson: 2904
title: Download: one word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Download is a verb and a noun. As a verb, it means to copy a file, game, music or app from the internet onto your computer, tablet or phone. As a noun, a download is the thing you copied. The verb changes too: downloads, downloaded, downloading.
explain: Read the words around it to find which meaning you need. «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat for an online game» tells you she copied something from the internet, because the cheat came from a site. Its opposite is upload, which sends your file from your device to the internet.
explain: Look for phrases to help: download an app, free download, download speed, download a file. Then swap your meaning into the sentence. "I copied the game from the internet" still makes sense, so download means copy from the internet here.
fact: Download means to copy a file, game, music or app from the internet onto a device.
fact: Upload is the opposite: it sends your file from your device to the internet.
fact: «Download» is a verb when it is an action, and a noun when it means the thing you copied.
fact: Download time is the file size divided by the speed: «600 megabytes at 10 megabytes per second takes 60 seconds.»
fact: Only download from trusted places, with an adult's permission, because some downloads contain viruses or cost money.
exercise: «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat for an online game.» What does downloaded mean here? | Paid for a game in a shop | *Copied from the internet onto her computer | Played a game with friends | Sent her own game to the internet
exercise: «600 megabytes at 10 megabytes per second takes 60 seconds.» How long is the download time? | *60 seconds | 600 seconds | 10 seconds | 6 seconds
exercise: What is the opposite of download? | Install | *Upload | Print | Delete
test: Which phrase is about getting a file from the internet? | *Download an app | Upload a photo | Share a video | Print a page
test: Which sentence uses download as a noun? | The teacher asked us to download the file | Ella will download the game tonight | *The free download took only a minute | We downloaded music yesterday
exam: Why should you only download from trusted places, with an adult's permission? | Because the internet cannot be used at home | *Because some downloads contain viruses or cost money | Because trusted places are always free | Because downloads are always slow
